<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=antikythera-mechanism">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Science and discovery</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antikythera mechanism</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Antikythera mechanism is an ancient Greek hand-powered orrery, a geared model of the Solar System, built in the 2nd century BCE and recovered in 1901 from a shipwreck off the Greek island of Antikythera. The oldest known example of an analogue computer, it could predict astronomical positions and eclipses decades in advance and track the four-year cycle of the ancient Olympic Games. Scans made in 2005 suggest that it had 35 meshing bronze gears. Its 82 fragments are kept at the National Archaeological Museum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antikythera-mechanism.jpg" alt="Antikythera mechanism" width="320" height="285" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marsyas · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NAMA_Machine_d'Anticyth%C3%A8re_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>2nd century BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Found off Antikythera, Greece</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd><a href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Its date and place of making are disputed: estimates run from 205 to 87 BCE, and Corinth’s colonies, Pergamon and Rhodes have been proposed.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-astronomy">Babylonian astronomy<span>c. 1800 BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=antikythera-mechanism">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
